<title>SINGAPORE: Samsung buys stake in Korean unit of HPL.</title>
<headline>Samsung buys stake in Korean unit of HPL.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Corporation has agreed to buy a 49 percent stake in HPL-21 Korea from a subsidiary company of Hotel Properties Ltd (HPL), according to a statement from HPL on Tuesday.</p>
<p>After the deal HPL-21 Holdings Ltd, part of the HPL group, will own the remaining 51 percent of HPL-21 Korea.</p>
<p>HPL-21 Korea operates retail boutique stores in Korea.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
